[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# Enrollment troubleshooting (/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting)\n\n\n\nDiagnose one operation and device at a time. Record the DMS/APS, endpoint, time, HTTP code, presented serial and CSR CN. Retain the response without including private keys or webhook credentials in the report.\n\nDiagnostics and compatibility [#diagnostics-and-compatibility]\n\nError codes and diagnostics [#error-codes-and-diagnostics]\n\nThe EST controller normally returns 400 when rejecting input and 500 when the service rejects or fails the operation. A 500 can also represent a policy denial; it does not mean retrying is safe. Gateway can produce its own codes and bodies. Examine the actual body and persisted result.\n\n| Symptom or message                                          | What to check                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| curl rejects TLS, name or issuer                            | URL, clock, server SAN and approved root in `est-trust.pem`. Resolve trust in [Deployment](/docs/deployment/troubleshooting); do not skip verification. |\n| 404 or missing APS                                          | Public route `/.well-known/est/{DMS_ID}/{operation}` and existing DMS. APS is not the service name.                                                     |\n| 400, CSR or format error                                    | `Content-Type: application/pkcs10`, Base64 of DER, valid signature and a body preserved without double encoding.                                        |\n| Missing credential or invalid certificate                   | Operation mode, validating CA, dates, revocation and credential delivery by Gateway. Do not confuse server TLS trust with the bootstrap CA.             |\n| Webhook denies, times out or responds without authorization | Configuration, connectivity and JSON response with `authorized: true`. There is no automatic fallback to `NO_AUTH`.                                     |\n| `device not preregistered`                                  | PRE\\_REGISTRATION requires an existing inventory entry.                                                                                                 |\n| `forbiddenNewEnrollment`                                    | An existing device requires replacement to be enabled, even in No Identity. Investigate before enabling the flag.                                       |\n| Different owning DMS                                        | CN/ID, global inventory and owning DMS; do not reuse an ID from another context.                                                                        |\n| `invalid RawSubject bytes`                                  | CSR subject versus the current certificate. Preserve its attributes as well as its CN.                                                                  |\n| `invalid reenroll window`                                   | Current identity's NotAfter and reenrollment\\_delta. Alert thresholds do not change that window.                                                        |\n| Current certificate revoked                                 | Renewal rejected; prepare authorized recovery according to the cause.                                                                                   |\n| CA, profile or signing error                                | Active CA, available key, selected profile and restrictions. Successful cacerts does not prove issuance.                                                |\n| HTTP 200 without a device connection                        | Installed pair, chain, uses, consumer trust and permissions. Also check the slot and history.                                                           |\n| Timeout or error after issuance                             | New certificates, current slot and previous identity's state before retrying.                                                                           |\n\nCompatibility notes [#compatibility-notes]\n\nThe examples use the contract of the [examined backend](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview#contract-version). Do not automatically attribute that behavior to another release. Check the saved renewal mode after migration and Gateway behavior with expired certificates and the bootstrap CA.\n\nThe default response is Base64-encoded DER PKCS#7; PEM through `Accept: application/x-pem-file` is a Lamassu extension. ServerKeyGen returns multipart and requires handling each part separately. See the [EST reference](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/est-reference).\n\nEST enrollment fails [#est-enrollment-fails]\n\n1. Check HTTPS with the approved root and query cacerts for the correct APS.\n2. Review the saved DMS: protocol, registration, authentication for that operation, CA, profile and window.\n3. Verify the CSR locally and relate its CN to the inventory.\n4. Make one request, save headers/body and query the device and certificates.\n5. If you receive an identity, check the key, subject, use and connection with the consumer.\n\nExternal bootstrap revocation checks have limitations: absence of evidence can be accepted, and OCSP Unknown does not cause the same rejection as Revoked. Do not assume a policy that rejects every uncertainty. An intermediate CA in the TLS chain does not prove that the entire chain reached the DMS validator either.\n\nFor logs, networking, pods or Gateway headers, continue in [Deployment troubleshooting](/docs/deployment/troubleshooting). For identities issued, revoked or bound partially, use [Renewal and recovery](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/renewal-and-recovery) and [Devices and identities](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/device-management).\n"]
